abstract: >
  The DIINA (Dynamic Inhibitory Neural Architecture) framework represents
  a novel approach to multilingual processing by integrating dual-path 
  (Fast Conv1D and Slow SSM/Attention) neural architectures with a 
  Linguistic Inhibition Gate (LIG). This repository provides the 
  core implementation, reproducibility telemetry, and benchmark 
  evaluation suite.
